  identity: "binary_operand_beside_a_block_headed_operand_is_dropped_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a binary expression whose right operand is block-headed lowers to that operand alone, and normalize ACCEPTS the module** (INVALID STATE: the lowered body of `t && match w {..}`, `t || match w {..}`, `t && u && match w {..}` and `t && if c {..} else {..}` is the match or if by itself. The left operands and the operators are gone, with no diagnostic.) The function then answers the block's value whatever `t` is. That is a wrong answer which type-checks: both sides are Bool. A name in the dropped operand never reaches resolve, so an undeclared one is accepted.",
    "RECEIPTS. Fixtures, traced by a scratch normalized-tree dump over `v2.compiler.program_assembly` `program_assembly_phase_normalize` at main 8bf4b66774c. All four forms above lower to the block alone. The block as LEFT operand (`match w {..} && t`) and the parenthesised form (`t && (match w {..})`) are REFUSED at normalize, not dropped, so the class is the unparenthesised block-headed right operand. Census: `v2.compiler.reference_conservation_census` `reference_conservation_census_for_paths` over `reference_conservation_stratified_sample_paths` at 69e0bb7566e. About 113 of the 3,472 atoms absent in accepted modules sit before or inside such a chain; this is a source-position heuristic, so the count is approximate. The densest file is `test.claim.codex_package_delivery_wet_witness_test`, whose witnesses are `&& match ..` chains; there a claim can hold on its last conjunct alone.",
    "WHERE: NOT YET LOCATED to a symbol. The route is `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold`'s operator-expression reading of a binary_expr whose right projection starts with a match_expr or if_expr. This row names the shape and the specimen, and the reader that drops the left operands is the next thing to cite. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: not `lowering_accessor_collapses_a_sequence_operand`, which keeps the LEFT element of an operand; here the left operands are what is lost. Not gunbc#11911, which is a parse-order defect where a block heading a && chain could not parse. Here the parse accepts and lowering drops.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silent wrongness). CEILING: structurally guaranteed. A binary expression lowers to an application of its operator over every operand, or refuses at the operand it could not read. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: v2 body lowering reads a binary chain whose right operand is a match or if as the full operator application. No lane owns it as of 2026-09-25: bright-boar-848's fold-cleanup lane declined it. The specimens `a_binary_operand_beside_a_match_reaches_resolve` and `a_binary_operand_beside_an_if_reaches_resolve` are enrolled expected-red. Their control `a_binary_operand_beside_a_name_reaches_resolve` is green.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.accepted_module_silent_drop", decl_name: "a_binary_operand_beside_a_match_reaches_resolve", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.accepted_module_silent_drop", decl_name: "a_binary_operand_beside_an_if_reaches_resolve", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.accepted_module_silent_drop", decl_name: "a_binary_operand_beside_a_name_reaches_resolve", field: WholeDeclaration },
